// data-layer-regex-sql-parsing, PENDING part (not read by the converter): A2 of regex-pattern-<k> for an f-string
// host with an interpolation. Merge into data-layer-regex-sql-parsing.rr once fstring_template is bound, replacing
// its A2 rule `rsp_text(x, v) :- rsp_fhost(x), value(x, v), value_type_of(x, "str").` (the template subsumes it).
//
// Waits on: W's `parse: {grammar: pythonFString, interpolation: marker}` root value (literal/python_fstring.rs::parse)
// of n, an f-string, a concatenated_string with an f-string part, or a format_specifier: the decoded literal text,
// each interpolation replaced by marker, a debug field's `expr =` source kept as literal; no row where W's parse
// gives no tree (not a JoinedStr, bytes, or Unknown). The marker is a column so one relation serves every policy's
// marker; the engine need bind only the constants programs pass (here "{...}"). It cannot be built in the file:
// joining the pieces by recursion along their index is a string-building cycle (UnboundedValueCycle), and an
// ordered `join` is not lowered.

.decl fstring_template(n: node, marker: symbol, v: symbol)

rsp_text(x, v) :- rsp_fhost(x), fstring_template(x, "{...}", v).
